---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'prerequisites', label: 'Prerequisites' },
  { id: 'network-info', label: 'Network Information' },
  { id: 'getting-started', label: 'Getting Started' },
  { id: 'running-nodes', label: 'Running Nodes' },
  { id: 'becoming-validator', label: 'Becoming a Validator' },
  { id: 'node-management', label: 'Node Management' },
];
---

<Layout title="Documentation - LAB Chain" description="Complete guide to running nodes on the LAB Chain network. Learn how to set up Execution Layer, Beacon, and Validator nodes.">
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <!-- Mobile Sidebar Toggle -->
    <button class="docs-mobile-toggle" id="docsSidebarToggle" aria-label="Toggle documentation menu">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <line x1="3" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"></line>
        <line x1="3" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"></line>
        <line x1="3" y1="18" x2="21" y2="18"></line>
      </svg>
      <span>Menu</span>
    </button>

    <!-- Sidebar Overlay -->
    <div class="docs-sidebar-overlay" id="docsSidebarOverlay"></div>

    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="docs-sidebar" id="docsSidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-content">
        <div class="sidebar-header-mobile">
          <h3>Documentation</h3>
          <button class="sidebar-close-btn" id="docsSidebarClose" aria-label="Close menu">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line>
              <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        <h3 class="sidebar-title-desktop">Documentation</h3>
        <nav class="sidebar-nav">
          {sections.map((section) => (
            <a href={`#${section.id}`} class="sidebar-link">
              {section.label}
            </a>
          ))}
        </nav>
        <div class="sidebar-cta">
          <a href="https://github.com/labchain5222/labchain" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M9 19c-5 1.5-5-2.5-7-3m14 6v-3.87a3.37 3.37 0 0 0-.94-2.61c3.14-.35 6.44-1.54 6.44-7A5.44 5.44 0 0 0 20 4.77 5.07 5.07 0 0 0 19.91 1S18.73.65 16 2.48a13.38 13.38 0 0 0-7 0C6.27.65 5.09 1 5.09 1A5.07 5.07 0 0 0 5 4.77a5.44 5.44 0 0 0-1.5 3.78c0 5.42 3.3 6.61 6.44 7A3.37 3.37 0 0 0 9 18.13V22"></path>
            </svg>
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="docs-main">
      <div class="docs-content">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="docs-header">
          <div class="breadcrumb">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline>
            </svg>
            <span>Documentation</span>
          </div>
          <h1>LAB Chain - Join the Network</h1>
          <p class="docs-intro">
            Welcome to LAB Chain! This guide will help you join our network as a node operator or validator.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Overview Section -->
        <section id="overview" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Overview</h2>
          <p>LAB Chain is a Proof-of-Stake Ethereum network. There are three types of nodes you can run:</p>

          <div class="node-types-grid">
            <div class="node-type-card">
              <div class="node-type-icon">
                <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                  <line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"></line>
                  <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"></line>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4>Full Node</h4>
              <p>Runs EL + CL together. You want to run your own complete node.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="node-type-card">
              <div class="node-type-icon">
                <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
                  <polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4>Beacon Node</h4>
              <p>Runs CL only. You have access to an external EL.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="node-type-card">
              <div class="node-type-icon">
                <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4>Validator</h4>
              <p>Runs VC only. You have access to an external Beacon Node and want to validate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>Components</h3>
          <div class="info-box">
            <p><strong>Execution Layer (EL):</strong> Reth - processes transactions and smart contracts</p>
            <p><strong>Consensus Layer (CL):</strong> Lighthouse Beacon Node - handles proof-of-stake consensus</p>
            <p><strong>Validator Client (VC):</strong> Lighthouse VC - proposes and attests to blocks</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Prerequisites Section -->
        <section id="prerequisites" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
          <p>Before you begin, make sure you have:</p>

          <h3>1. Docker & Docker Compose</h3>
          <p>Install Docker:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Create a new user and grant docker permissions:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Create new user (replace 'nodeuser' with your preferred username)
sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash nodeuser
# Add user to docker group
sudo usermod -aG docker nodeuser
# Switch to new user
su - nodeuser</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash nodeuser\nsudo usermod -aG docker nodeuser\nsu - nodeuser'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Verify installation:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>docker --version
docker compose version</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='docker --version\ndocker compose version'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>2. Foundry (for validators only)</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Install Foundry
curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash
foundryup
# Verify installation
cast --version</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash\nfoundryup\ncast --version'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>3. jq (for validators only)</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># macOS
brew install jq
# Ubuntu/Debian
sudo apt install jq</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='brew install jq'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>4. Minimum Hardware</h3>
          <div class="requirements-grid">
            <div class="req-item">
              <strong>CPU</strong>
              <p>4 cores</p>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <strong>RAM</strong>
              <p>8 GB</p>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <strong>Storage</strong>
              <p>100 GB SSD</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>5. Network Ports (open in your firewall)</h3>

          <div class="info-box">
            <h4>Do you need to open these ports?</h4>
            <p><strong>Private Node (your own use):</strong> No, ports don't need to be opened publicly. Your node can still connect to other nodes and sync properly.</p>
            <p><strong>Public Node (bootnode or community node):</strong> Yes, ports must be opened publicly so other nodes can discover and connect to your node.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="requirements-grid">
            <div class="req-item">
              <strong>30303</strong>
              <p>TCP/UDP - EL peer discovery</p>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <strong>9000</strong>
              <p>TCP/UDP - CL peer discovery</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3>6. NTP Time Synchronization</h3>
          <p>Blockchain nodes require accurate system time for proper consensus operation. Configure your server to use NTP:</p>

          <p><strong>Ubuntu/Debian:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>sudo apt install chrony
sudo systemctl enable chrony
sudo systemctl start chrony

# Verify time sync
chronyc tracking</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='sudo apt install chrony\nsudo systemctl enable chrony\nsudo systemctl start chrony\nchronyc tracking'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>macOS (most systems are already configured):</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>brew install chrony
sudo brew services start chrony

# Verify time sync
chronyc tracking</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='brew install chrony\nsudo brew services start chrony\nchronyc tracking'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Verify time is synchronized (Linux):</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>timedatectl status
# Should show: "System clock synchronized: yes"</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="timedatectl status">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Network Information Section -->
        <section id="network-info" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Network Information</h2>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Parameter</th>
                  <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Network Name</td>
                  <td><code>lab-chain</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Chain ID</td>
                  <td><code>5222</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Slot Duration</td>
                  <td><code>12 seconds</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Deposit Contract</td>
                  <td><code>0x5454545454545454545454545454545454545454</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Explorer</td>
                  <td><a href="https://explorer.labchain.la" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://explorer.labchain.la</a></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Getting Started Section -->
        <section id="getting-started" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Getting Started</h2>
          <p>Follow these steps to set up your environment before running any node.</p>

          <h3>Step 1: Clone the Repository</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>git clone https://github.com/labchain5222/labchain
cd labchain</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="git clone https://github.com/labchain5222/labchain\ncd labchain">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Step 2: Create Docker Network</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>docker network create labchain-net</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="docker network create labchain-net">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Step 3: Generate JWT Secret</h3>
          <p>The JWT secret secures communication between EL and CL.</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>mkdir -p config/jwt
openssl rand -hex 32 > config/jwt/jwtsecret</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='mkdir -p config/jwt\nopenssl rand -hex 32 > config/jwt/jwtsecret'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="info-box success">
            <h4>You're Ready!</h4>
            <p>You're now ready to run nodes!</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Running Nodes Section -->
        <section id="running-nodes" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Running Nodes</h2>
          <p>Use the <code>./node.sh</code> script to configure and manage all nodes.</p>

          <div class="info-box">
            <h4>Note: Optional Configuration</h4>
            <p>The default configuration is pre-configured and ready to use. You can simply press Enter to accept defaults during <code>./node.sh init</code>, or skip the init step entirely and start nodes directly.</p>
          </div>

          <h3>Run Execution Layer (EL)</h3>

          <p><strong>1. Configure EL (optional - defaults are ready to use):</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh init el</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh init el">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Configuration options:</p>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Config</th>
                  <th>Default</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>JSON-RPC HTTP port</td>
                  <td><code>8545</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>WebSocket RPC port</td>
                  <td><code>8546</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Auth RPC port (engine API for CL)</td>
                  <td><code>8551</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>P2P networking port</td>
                  <td><code>30303</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Bootnode enode URL</td>
                  <td>Pre-configured</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p><strong>2. Start EL:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh start el</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh start el">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>3. Verify EL is running:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh logs el
# Test RPC
curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
--data '&#123;"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_blockNumber","params":[],"id":1&#125;' \
http://localhost:8545</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" --data \'&#123;"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_blockNumber","params":[],"id":1&#125;\' http://localhost:8545'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Run Consensus Layer (CL)</h3>

          <p><strong>1. Configure CL (optional - defaults are ready to use):</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh init cl</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh init cl">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Configuration options:</p>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Config</th>
                  <th>Default</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Execution engine endpoint</td>
                  <td><code>http://reth-node:8551</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Beacon HTTP API port</td>
                  <td><code>5052</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>P2P networking port</td>
                  <td><code>9000</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Target number of peers</td>
                  <td><code>64</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Your public IP for P2P discovery</td>
                  <td>Auto-detected</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Discovery protocol</td>
                  <td><code>enr</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Bootnode addresses</td>
                  <td>Pre-configured</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Sync mode</td>
                  <td><code>full</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Checkpoint sync URL</td>
                  <td>-</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h4>Choose Your Sync Mode</h4>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Mode</th>
                  <th>Speed</th>
                  <th>Storage</th>
                  <th>When to Use</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Full</strong></td>
                  <td>Slower (syncs from genesis)</td>
                  <td>More</td>
                  <td>Complete node with full history</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Checkpoint</strong></td>
                  <td>Fast (syncs from recent point)</td>
                  <td>Less</td>
                  <td>Quick startup, trusted checkpoint</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Full Sync (Default):</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># SYNC_MODE=full is set by default
# No additional configuration needed
./node.sh start cl</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh start cl">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Checkpoint Sync (Recommended for Faster Setup):</strong></p>
          <p>Set checkpoint sync mode during configuration:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh init cl
# Select: 2) checkpoint
# Enter checkpoint URL: https://checkpoin.labchain.la</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='./node.sh init cl\n# Select: 2) checkpoint\n# Enter checkpoint URL: https://checkpoin.labchain.la'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Or manually edit <code>CL/.env</code>:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># CL/.env
SYNC_MODE=checkpoint
CHECKPOINT_SYNC_URL=https://checkpoin.labchain.la</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="SYNC_MODE=checkpoint\nCHECKPOINT_SYNC_URL=https://checkpoin.labchain.la">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>2. Start CL:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh start cl</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh start cl">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p><strong>3. Verify CL is running:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh logs cl
# Test beacon API
curl http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/node/syncing</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="curl http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/node/syncing">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Becoming a Validator Section -->
        <section id="becoming-validator" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Becoming a Validator</h2>
          <p>To become a validator, you need to:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Have a running Beacon Node (CL)</li>
            <li>Generate validator keystores</li>
            <li>Deposit 32 LAB per validator</li>
            <li>Run the Validator Client (VC)</li>
          </ol>

          <h3>Step 1: Generate Validator Keystores</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>cd VC
./manage-validators.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cd VC\n./manage-validators.sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>The script will guide you through:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Number of validators to create (default: 1)</li>
            <li>Your LAB withdrawal address</li>
            <li>Starting validator index (default: 0)</li>
            <li>Output directories</li>
          </ol>

          <div class="info-box warning">
            <h4>Important: Save Your Mnemonic!</h4>
            <p>Save your mnemonic securely when prompted! This is the only way to recover your validator keys.</p>
          </div>

          <p>This creates:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>./output/deposits.json</code> - Deposit data for broadcasting</li>
            <li><code>./managed-keystores/validators/</code> - Keystore files</li>
            <li><code>./managed-keystores/secrets/</code> - Password files</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Step 2: Fund Your Validators (Deposit 32 LAB)</h3>
          <p>You need 32 LAB per validator. Use the deposit script:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./broadcast-deposits.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./broadcast-deposits.sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>The script will guide you through:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Path to deposits.json (default: ./output/deposits.json)</li>
            <li>RPC endpoint (default: http://localhost:8545)</li>
            <li>Sender address (your funded wallet)</li>
            <li>Private key (hidden input)</li>
            <li>Chain ID and deposit contract (pre-configured defaults)</li>
            <li>Dry-run option to preview before sending</li>
          </ol>

          <div class="info-box">
            <p>Each deposit costs 32 LAB. Wait for deposits to be processed (about 16-24 hours).</p>
          </div>

          <h3>Step 3: Configure and Start Validator Client</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>cd ..
# Configure VC (optional - defaults are ready to use)
./node.sh init vc</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='cd ..\n./node.sh init vc'>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Configuration options:</p>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Config</th>
                  <th>Default</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Beacon node REST API endpoints</td>
                  <td><code>http://lighthouse-bn:5052</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Fee recipient address</td>
                  <td><code>0x0000...0000</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Root directory for keystores</td>
                  <td><code>./managed-keystores</code></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Start VC
./node.sh start vc</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh start vc">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Step 4: Verify Your Validator</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>./node.sh logs vc</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh logs vc">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>Look for these messages in the logs:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>Enabled validator</code> - Your validator is loaded</li>
            <li><code>Successfully published attestation</code> - Validator is attesting (after activation)</li>
            <li><code>Successfully published block</code> - Validator proposed a block</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Exiting Validators (Withdraw Funds)</h3>
          <p>To exit your validator and withdraw all funds (stake + rewards), use the exit script:</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>cd VC
./exit-validators.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cd VC\n./exit-validators.sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p>The script will guide you through the process interactively:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Configure beacon node URL (default: http://localhost:5052)</li>
            <li>Configure keystore directory (default: ./managed-keystores)</li>
            <li>Select validators to exit (all, specific numbers, or by public key)</li>
            <li>Confirm the exit</li>
          </ol>

          <div class="info-box warning">
            <h4>Important: Irreversible</h4>
            <p>Voluntary exits are <strong>irreversible</strong>. After exit:</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Validator enters exit queue</li>
              <li>Exit processing (~27 hours minimum)</li>
              <li>Withdrawal delay (~27 hours after exit)</li>
              <li>Funds (32 LAB + rewards) sent to your withdrawal address</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Node Management Section -->
        <section id="node-management" class="docs-section">
          <h2>Node Management</h2>
          <p>The <code>./node.sh</code> script provides all commands for managing your nodes.</p>

          <h3>Commands</h3>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Command</th>
                  <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh init &lt;node&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>Configure a node interactively (optional)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh start &lt;node&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>Start a node</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh stop &lt;node&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>Stop a node</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh restart &lt;node&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>Restart a node</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh logs &lt;node&gt;</code></td>
                  <td>View node logs (follow mode)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh status</code></td>
                  <td>Show status of all nodes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>./node.sh health</code></td>
                  <td>Check network health</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3>Node Options</h3>
          <div class="params-table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Node</th>
                  <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>el</code></td>
                  <td>Execution Layer (Reth)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>cl</code></td>
                  <td>Consensus Layer (Lighthouse Beacon)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>vc</code></td>
                  <td>Validator Client (Lighthouse VC)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>all</code></td>
                  <td>All nodes</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3>Examples</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Start EL with default settings
./node.sh start el

# Start all nodes
./node.sh start all

# Stop validator client
./node.sh stop vc

# View CL logs
./node.sh logs cl

# Check status of all nodes
./node.sh status

# Restart CL
./node.sh restart cl</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="./node.sh start el">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Check Sync Status</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># EL sync status
curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
--data '&#123;"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_syncing","params":[],"id":1&#125;' \
http://localhost:8545

# CL sync status
curl http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/node/syncing</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="curl -X POST">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Get Current Block/Slot</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Current EL block
curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
--data '&#123;"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_blockNumber","params":[],"id":1&#125;' \
http://localhost:8545

# Current CL slot
curl http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/beacon/headers/head</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="curl -X POST">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Get Bootnode Information</h3>
          <p>If you're running a bootnode and need to share connection info with other nodes:</p>

          <p><strong>Get EL Bootnode Enode:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>cd EL
./get-bootnode-enode.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cd EL\n./get-bootnode-enode.sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p>This returns the enode URL (e.g., <code>enode://abc123...@IP:30303</code>) that other EL nodes can use to connect.</p>

          <div class="info-box">
            <p>When sharing bootnode addresses with other operators, replace <code>IP</code> with your server's public IP address so they can connect to your node.</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Get CL Bootnode ENR:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code>cd CL
./get-bootnode-enr.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="cd CL\n./get-bootnode-enr.sh">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p>This returns the ENR record (e.g., <code>enr:-...</code>) that other CL nodes can use for peer discovery.</p>

          <p><strong>Get CL Bootnode libp2p Address:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Get libp2p multiaddr from beacon node
curl -s http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/node/identity | jq -r '.data.p2p_addresses&#91;0&#93;'</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy='curl -s http://localhost:5052/eth/v1/node/identity | jq -r \'.data.p2p_addresses&#91;0&#93;\''>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p>This returns the libp2p multiaddr (e.g., <code>/ip4/IP/tcp/9000/p2p/PEER_ID</code>) for nodes using libp2p discovery mode.</p>

          <div class="info-box">
            <p>When sharing bootnode addresses with other operators, replace <code>IP</code> with your server's public IP address so they can connect to your node.</p>
          </div>

          <p><strong>Custom RPC URLs:</strong></p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <code># Custom EL RPC
RPC_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8545 ./get-bootnode-enode.sh

# Custom CL RPC
RPC_URL=http://192.168.1.100:5052 ./get-bootnode-enr.sh</code>
            <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="RPC_URL=http://192.168.1.100:8545">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
                <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

